---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/baseLayout.astro";
import Button from "../components/button.astro";

const pageTitle = "Terms of Use";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
 
<BaseLayout
title="Terms of Use">

<nav class="navigation-controls">
    <Button  variant="outline" size="xs" theme="brown" class="back-button" onclick="history.length > 1 ? history.back() : window.location.href='/events'"> ← Previous Page </Button>
</nav>

<h1> Terms of Use</h1>
<section class="frame-fence">


3. Terms of Use (The "Ground Rules")
While the Privacy Policy is about data, the Terms of Use (ToS) are about behavior and contracts.

Acceptance: A statement that by using the site, they agree to these terms.

Intellectual Property: Stating that the content on the site (logos, text, designs) belongs to you.

User Conduct: No hacking, scraping, or posting abusive content.

Limitation of Liability: You aren't responsible if the site goes down or if they lose data using your service.

Governing Law: Explicitly state: "These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales."

</section>

</BaseLayout>